Spacers (Aerochamber®)
When the medication comes out of the inhaler, it may be deposited 
on the back of the throat and not reach the lungs or the casualty 
may be gasping for air and unable to hold their breath. To deal 
with this, use a spacer if available. It traps the particles of the spray, 
allowing the casualty to inhale more effectively over several breaths.
Spacers make it simple to inhale the medication, and should always 
be used when available. Small children and other casualties who 
have difficulties coordinating proper inhalation with the release of 
the medication will often have spacers with them.
