• Stabilize the affected body part only if doing so does not cause additional pain; do not try to 
force a deformed joint back into place as this may cause further damage. 
• Many victims of musculoskeletal injury will assume a position of comfort- allow them to do so if 
this decreases their pain. 
• Remember the acronym RICE when treating injured extremities (arms and legs, feet and hands): 
o Rest any injured joint 
o Apply a cold pack or Ice if available to reduce swelling and control pain 
o Apply Compression (an elastic bandage) for any sprains or strains 
o Elevate the injured body part above the heart to reduce swelling 
